  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Workforce",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nDSH Workforce is a local Agent organization and project collaboration plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH). It brings long-lived Agents, project memberships, Work conversations, management conversations, and structured Meetings into one Workforce experience while continuing to use DSH for models, Tools, Skills, Sessions, and runtime execution.\n\nCurrent version: `V0.1.1`"
    },
    {
      "section": "Highlights",
      "text": "- WorkforceCenter manages long-lived Agent profiles, personas, model bindings, Tools, and Skills across projects.\n- Project Sidebar shows the Workforce Project, Agents, Work, and Meetings associated with the active Workspace.\n- Each Project × Agent has one reusable Work conversation and one management conversation.\n- Project facts remain in the project directory, while long-lived Agent profiles remain in the user-level WorkforceCenter.\n- Project Meetings provide participants, discussion rounds, explicit responses, and durable decisions without an external Room plugin.\n- V0.1.1 is local-first, single-user, and backed by SQLite."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js 24\n- DeepSeek Harness `>=0.1.1-rc.2`\n\nWorkforce never asks users to enter a model provider, API key, or model name inside the plugin. DSH remains the source of truth for model catalogs and provider configuration. If a DSH model source becomes unavailable, Workforce asks the user to rebind the Agent."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Pin release tags so unverified upstream changes cannot silently alter a working profile:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:esonx/dsh-workforce#v0.1.1\ndsh web\n```\n\nYou can also install the tarball attached to the GitHub Release:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-workforce-0.1.1.tgz\ndsh web\n```\n\nSee [Installation and upgrades](docs/INSTALLATION.md) for the complete procedure."
    },
    {
      "section": "Get started",
      "text": "1. Start DSH Web normally and open a Workspace.\n2. Select **Workforce** in the lower-left navigation.\n3. If the active Workspace is not yet a Workforce Project, select **Go!**.\n4. Open **WorkforceCenter** to create or configure an Agent.\n5. Add Agents to the current project, then open a management or Work conversation, or create a Meeting."
    },
    {
      "section": "Get started",
      "text": "The project-local `.workforce/` directory stores project facts. `workforce-center/center.sqlite` under the user's DSH Home stores long-lived Agent profiles. Neither location stores provider API keys. See the [User guide](docs/USER_GUIDE.md) for backup and recovery guidance."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security boundary",
      "text": "- V0.1.1 assumes one local user operating DSH. It does not provide multi-user login, enterprise RBAC, or remote service deployment.\n- DSH and plugins installed in the same Profile share a trusted host boundary. Do not install untrusted plugins in that Profile.\n- loopback/Origin/`trustedHosts` constrain browser transport; they are not Host user authentication.\n- DSH `allowed-once` authorizes only the current execution; it is not a persistent or replayable Host management capability.\n- External Workspace, Session, and Preset identifiers are never Workforce organization primary keys.\n- The browser cannot nominate a Project root, Session ID, provider key, or runtime authorization identity.\n- Cross-Project access is denied by default. Unknown or partially completed external operations are never replayed automatically."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security boundary",
      "text": "See [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) to report a security issue."
    },
    {
      "section": "V0.1.1 limitations",
      "text": "- Local, single-user operation only; multi-user accounts, multiple instances, and shared-database deployments are unsupported.\n- Each Project × Agent can have at most one active Work conversation and one active management conversation. Historical conversation expansion is planned for a later version.\n- Meetings are project-local structured collaboration records; free-form Room/private-chat channels are not part of the V1 product surface.\n- PRD and Dev/Taskboard are still future Sidebar entry points.\n- Memory V1 provides scoped long-term Agent memory extraction, consolidation, retrieval, UI governance, and policy-controlled Global promotion. Knowledge-base imports are not included.\n- DSH is evolving quickly. Validate Workforce in a test Profile before upgrading DSH in a working environment."
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture boundary",
      "text": "Workforce owns long-lived Agents, Project Memberships, Work, Meetings, external bindings, and its V1 Memory engine. DSH continues to own model execution and Sessions; task facts remain with their authoritative project plugin. See the [Architecture overview](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uninstall",
